cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "USearchWiki: An Open, Searchable Atlas of Wiki-Style and Scholarly Text"
message: "If you use this dataset, please cite it as below."
type: dataset
license: Apache-2.0
version: 3.0.0
repository-code: https://github.com/unum-cloud/USearchWiki
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.23977284
abstract: >-
  An open, searchable atlas of wiki-style and scholarly text, including Wikipedia in every
  language and the arXiv, bioRxiv and medRxiv preprint servers under each paper's own license.
  Every document is one Parquet row under a permanent key, with its sections, original markup
  and rendered text inside it, while embeddings from several models, links resolved to
  cross-language Wikidata entities and the dates and places each passage mentions are added
  beside the same rows, together with USearch graphs that search documents and sections,
  including late-interaction MaxSim. It is distributed as row-aligned Parquet shards with one
  file per embedding model and graph files on AWS S3, for researchers, retrieval pipelines and
  agents that search text across languages and disciplines.
keywords:
  - wikipedia
  - scholarly literature
  - information retrieval
  - semantic search
  - multilingual embeddings
  - entity linking
  - vector search
  - open data

